# The build context is the repository root (deploy/docker-compose.yml, context: ..),
# so without this file every image build sends node_modules, git history and
# whatever databases happen to be on the developer's machine.
#
# The databases matter most: `COPY orchestrator/ /app/` used to carry aidemo.db,
# unify.db and any other *.db in that directory into the image - demo data at
# best, a developer's real corpus at worst. The decision store belongs on the
# /data volume and nowhere else (playbook §9).
.git
.claude
.cursor
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.db
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal
**/*.jsonl
**/*.log
**/data
frontend/dist
docs/*.png
docs/*.docx
deploy/.env
deploy/config/*
*.md
